	<key>readme</key>
	<string>Simple Currency — currency conversion by code or by name, in English and Spanish.

USAGE
cur                            your favourites against the base currency
cur 100 usd                    100 US dollars to the base currency
cur 100 yuan                   by name — codes are optional
cur 1,000,000 clp a dolares    «a», «en» or «to» set the direction
cur usd yuan                   between two currencies, both ways
cur peso                       ambiguous names show a picker (⇥ completes)
cur-add / cur-rm               choose the favourites you compare against
cur-help                       every example

↩ copies the result · ⌥ the full expression · ⌘ the number only.
The rates row at the bottom is clickable: ↩ on it downloads fresh rates and reopens Alfred with the same query.

LANGUAGES
The interface follows the macOS language (English or Spanish); override it in Configure → Interface language. Currency names are searchable in both languages, with or without accents, singular or plural: dollar, dólares, chilean peso, peso chileno, yuan, corona sueca, swiss franc.

ESPAÑOL
cur                            tus favoritas contra la moneda principal
cur 100 usd                    100 dólares a la moneda principal
cur 100 yuan                   por nombre, sin códigos
cur 1.000.000 clp a dolares    con «a» o «en» fijas la dirección
cur-add / cur-rm               elegir las favoritas contra las que se compara

DATA &amp; PRIVACY
Rates from open.er-api.com (no API key), cached on disk for an hour, with currency-api as a fallback. Nothing else leaves your Mac. Requires Python 3 (/usr/bin/python3, included with the Command Line Tools). Based on Coinc by Tomy Hsieh (MIT); the flag icons come from the same project.
</string>
